# AI Identity

@bootstrap.identity

Purpose:
  Define the AI's identity within this project:
  - Which project it is working on
  - What environment it operates in
  - What role it plays
  - What capabilities it has

project:
    @project.sddra-ai

environment:
    development

agent:
    implementation-agent

role:
    backend-engineer

capabilities:
    read: code, documentation, tests
    write: code, tests, documentation
    execute: go test, go build, docker
    tools: read_file, write_file, run_tests

## Identity Resolution

AI resolves identity during bootstrap phase 1 (WHO AM I?).
Identity determines which INDEX.sdd to load and which domain indexes
to follow.

## Role Mapping

  role: backend-engineer
    → loads: @architecture.backend
    → loads: @skill.go, @skill.postgres, @skill.docker
    → loads: @domain.payment, @domain.provider

  role: reviewer
    → loads: @protocol.review-standards
    → loads: @skill.code-review

  role: researcher
    → loads: @skill.research
    → loads: @concept.*

Navigation:
  Parent: @INDEX.sdd
  Authority: @authority.sdd
  Project: @../project/INDEX.sdd
  Skills: @../skills/INDEX.sdd
  Architecture: @../architecture/INDEX.sdd

State: +
